# Personal GitHub user (Dr0na)

This repository is a **personal** GitHub project under the **`Dr0na`** account.

## Git remotes and push or pull

- Use **`Dr0na`** as the GitHub identity for **`origin`** and related remotes.
- Prefer HTTPS with embedded user (avoids accidental rewrite to SSH if global
  `insteadOf` maps plain `https://github.com/` to SSH):

  `https://Dr0na@github.com/Dr0na/<repository>.git`

- Alternative: SSH form `git@github.com:Dr0na/<repository>.git` when SSH keys
  for **Dr0na** are configured on the machine.

- Do **not** change `origin` to another user (for example `vnalwar`) unless the
  user explicitly asks to move, fork, or transfer the repo.

## GitHub CLI and credentials

- For `gh auth login`, `gh pr`, `gh repo`, and similar actions for **this**
  project, assume the active GitHub account should be **`Dr0na`**.
- If `gh auth status` shows an invalid token for **Dr0na**, tell the user to run
  `gh auth logout -h github.com -u Dr0na` then `gh auth login` as **Dr0na**,
  and use `gh auth switch -u Dr0na` when multiple accounts exist.

## Commits (optional)

- If the user asks to set `user.name` / `user.email` for this repo to match
  **Dr0na**, use the name and email they provide; do not invent an email.

## Links in docs

- Prefer GitHub URLs under `github.com/Dr0na/` when linking this project.
